India has been ranked ninth among the countries most severely impacted by climate-related catastrophes over the past three decades, according to the latest Climate Risk Index (CRI) report published by Germanwatch, a non-governmental organization based in Bonn.

The report, which was unveiled on the second day of the ongoing COP30 climate summit in Belém, Brazil, was compiled through an analysis of current and past climate data available in public forums. In the most recent index, completed in 2023, India secured the eighth position.

