data.fused_content:
BOISE COUNTY, Idaho — A section of State Highway 21, known as "Avalanche Alley," has reopened after adverse weather delayed rock scaling efforts required due to a major rockslide earlier this month.

The Idaho Transportation Department (ITD) announced on Tuesday that Highway 21 is now open from milepost 93.7 near Grandjean to milepost 105.5 at Banner Summit. This portion of the road is frequently closed throughout the winter season due to avalanche threats or actual snowslides blocking the route.

The initial rockslide, which occurred overnight on December 9, forced the closure of the highway between Sourdough and Banner Summit. The road briefly resumed operations on December 12 with fewer lanes and enhanced safety protocols but was subsequently shut down again for further rock scaling activities.

