The hikers allegedly ignored weather advisories issued for Typhoon Wipha and ended up stranded on a mountain in Shenzhen's Dapeng New Area. Following an exhausting 12-hour search and rescue effort, they were relocated to safety.

As stipulated by the city's regulation on the prevention and control of national disasters, fines may be levied between 5,000 to 20,000 yuan for accessing designated natural disaster danger zones with access restrictions. Each of the two offenders received a fine of 5,000 yuan. According to the guidelines, individuals may also be accountable for the expenses related to rescue operations.

