Severe rainfall has led to at least 60 deaths across northern China since late July, including in the capital city of Beijing, where 30 fatalities were reported. Flood warnings have been issued in 11 provinces as heavy rains persist.

Chinese President Xi Jinping has commanded rescue efforts to be carried out with complete dedication and maximum exertion to locate the missing individuals. He directed all regions to “resolutely overcome complacency” and strengthen efforts to identify risks in the face of frequent extreme weather.

Video released by Chinese fire officials on Weibo depicted rescuers leading villagers through rapidly flowing grey water. Images from the Gansu government showed roads blanketed with silt and sizable stones.

