A torrential downpour on Monday led to flooding and landslides, blocking a major highway and leaving over 200 local tourists stranded. Army helicopters were deployed to facilitate evacuation efforts. Several vehicles were engulfed by landslide debris, and three bodies have been recovered. Rescuers are using heavy equipment to search for missing tourists and residents.

Days prior, the National Disaster Management Authority issued a flood alert, advising against travel to northern regions due to the risks of landslides and road obstructions. Experts attribute the increase in extreme weather events in the area to the impacts of climate change. Officials have cautioned that another bout of severe weather, similar to the 2022 floods that inundated one-third of the nation and caused 1,737 fatalities, cannot be dismissed.
