Following severe rainfall, a massive mudslide demolished three homes in Brazzano di Cormons, near Gorizia, between Sunday night and Monday morning. The bodies of two individuals were retrieved by firefighters: Quirin Kuhnert, a 32-year-old German, and 83-year-old Guerrina Skocaj. Kuhnert perished while valiantly attempting to rescue Skocaj from her residence after recognizing the looming threat of the landslide. The area now stands as an immense heap of debris.

